  "body": "**Account failover, hibernation, and faster reloads**\n\n### Highlights\n\n- Automatically retry turns on the next pool account when one hits a usage limit, including for Desktop and SDK clients\n- Hibernate idle sessions to free memory, with measured RAM status and transparent wake on the next interaction\n- Reload and resume large sessions much faster by showing the local transcript immediately and sending only new history\n\n### Improvements\n\n- Support OpenAI Ultrafast speed tiers for GPT-6.1 Sol, with Fast commands and hotkeys that apply promptly\n- Show saved accounts, cached quotas, and available resets in the startup account router and usage cards\n- Polish usage cards with responsive gauges and compact Mil and Bil token totals\n- Offer additional OAuth accounts in the login picker and reauthenticate saved accounts from it\n- Show cache misses inline with more accurate cache reuse diagnostics\n- Show Jcode inference spending balance\n- Compress OpenAI and Anthropic request bodies to reduce upload time\n- Build the /model picker off the UI thread for large remote catalogs\n- Reconnect only changed MCP servers instead of restarting all of them\n- Simplify swarm mode by removing the task graph and defaulting swarm root effort to low\n\n### Fixes\n\n- Keep startup headers and account rows on a single line at narrow widths\n- Show usage-limit rejections clearly instead of stale quota bars\n- Fix forked sessions failing on replayed Anthropic web search blocks\n- Count Gemini thinking and tool-use tokens correctly in usage\n- Keep streamed OpenAI output when the completion payload arrives empty\n- Preserve token usage when requests are cancelled or fail\n- Fix Windows named-pipe connections hanging or failing on startup probes\n- Fix Firefox cold starts blocked by stale zombie processes\n- Collapse expanded pinned todos and restore overall progress display\n\n**Full changelog**: https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode/compare/v0.98.1...v0.99.0\n\n<!-- jcode-platform-availability:start -->\n## Platform availability\n\n- Linux x86_64: available\n- Linux aarch64: available\n- macOS Apple Silicon: available\n- macOS Intel: available\n- Windows x86_64: available\n- Windows ARM64: available\n- FreeBSD x86_64: available\n\nWindows executables are **unsigned**. Azure Artifact Signing is not configured and the repository's existing `WINDOWS_SIGNING_REQUIRED=false` override allowed unsigned publication. Windows may show publisher or SmartScreen warnings.\n<!-- jcode-platform-availability:end -->\n\n<!-- jcode-discord-announced:v0.99.0 -->\n",
